Specifically:

  * apply-seccomp
    The login sandbox installs and runs Anthropic's `apply-seccomp` seccomp-BPF
    helper. husk does not redistribute it: the install script downloads it,
    unmodified, from the @anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime package on the public npm
    registry at install time (see install-husk.sh). That package carries its own
    Apache-2.0 license terms.

  * Compute-node filesystem cage
    The SLURM broker's compute-node re-sandbox (slurm-broker/broker/src/settings.rs)
    is an independent Rust reimplementation adapted from sandbox-runtime's Linux
    filesystem model — read-default-allow / write-default-deny policy, credential
    masking, and bubblewrap (bwrap) argument construction. It contains no source
    code copied from sandbox-runtime; it reimplements the same approach.

